{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":184,"code_snippet":"live_run_signal(){ ctx_signals | grep -q '^live ' ; }","reasoning_trace":"Read op_confirm's only runtime gate (line 509) back to live_run_signal. Under set -o pipefail (line 46) grep -q exits on first match; ctx_signals forks jq between echos so its next echo takes SIGPIPE (141) and the function returns false. Reproduced in a scratch head checkout with marker + RUNNING state + LOA_UNATTENDED=1: confirm exit 0, row decided. With one signal: refused.","finding":"confirm gate fails open under two or more live-run signals","critique":"The gate is weakest exactly when the run is most clearly unattended.","remediation":"Collect ctx_signals into a variable, then test for a 'live ' line; same at validate-artifact.sh:559; add a two-signal bats case.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754","CWE-391"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":359,"code_snippet":"is_operator_call(){ [[ \"$(o recorded-by)\" == \"$OPERATOR_CMD\" ]]; }","reasoning_trace":"Traced every operator-only transition (confirm :508, decided reject :574, supersede :600-607, context --clear :716) to this one string compare. disable-model-invocation (decisions.md:4) fences the Skill tool only; settings.json has no Bash deny. Reproduced: agent-style new then confirm --recorded-by decisions-command on an interactive terminal -> decided_by operator. Dissent DISS-001 and DISS-C-001 (both HIGH) independently; DISS-C-002 shows the signal set is caller-controlled (CLAUDE_SESSION_ID=other flips unattended to interactive; reproduced).","finding":"operator authority is a self-asserted CLI flag; the model's Bash tool mints decided_by: operator","critique":"decisions.md:3 and :26-28 claim the model cannot invoke these operations; the control is prompt-level and a grep over prompt files.","remediation":"Bash permission deny rule for dec-write-lib.sh confirm / --recorded-by decisions-command / context --clear in settings.json, or a hook-minted token required by is_operator_call; time-based marker staleness; reword decisions.md.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-290","CWE-863","OWASP-A01:2021"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":642,"code_snippet":".decisions[] | walk(if type == \"string\" then rw else . end)","reasoning_trace":"import validates the pending file (:627) with rules that never forbid a decided row or a non-null decided_by in a pending file; imported ids are all 'touched' so verify_and_swap compares their content to nothing; the --base-file operator-row rule fires only under a live signal. Reproduced: hand-edited pending row (status decided, decided_by operator, two transitions with by operator:decisions-command) imported with exit 0 into the live ledger.","finding":"import appends hand-edited pending rows verbatim; a worktree agent lands a decided/operator row through the lead's import","critique":"The import is the trust boundary for worktree rows and performs no normalisation.","remediation":"Normalise on import (status open/proposed, decided_by null, regenerated transitions, reject operator: markers and recorded_by decisions-command); validator rule for pending rows; bats case.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-345","CWE-20"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":183,"code_snippet":"is_unattended(){ [[ -n \"$(ctx_signals)\" ]]; }","reasoning_trace":"ctx_signals emits 'prd prd-status' when the PRD **Status** line says autonomous/unattended (:177-180). is_unattended treats it as unattended; derive_attribution (:313-316) drops --answer-ref; confirm proceeds (:509 checks live only) and :538 records decided_by agent. Reproduced: decided_by agent, decided_by_ref null; operator reject refused (:575); operator supersede took the agent path (:600-611).","finding":"a PRD Status line saying autonomous strips the operator's attribution and disables operator reject","critique":"A planning-time, agent-writable line decides an attribution outcome.","remediation":"Operator-path decisions use live_run_signal only; keep the PRD hint for write defaults.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-807"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"completeness","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":271,"code_snippet":"[[ -f \"$TARGET\" ]] || die \"ledger not found: ${TARGET} (restore the tracked grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml)\"","reasoning_trace":"Searched the 39-file diff for grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml: referenced by the writer, .gitignore negation, validate-gitignore-state tracked_set and three bats setups, never added or bootstrapped; base .gitignore ignored it so it was not tracked before. Verified errexit semantics of the setup group: sed failure aborts before printf.","finding":"the tracked ledger file is neither shipped nor bootstrapped; every live write and three bats suites fail on a fresh clone","critique":"The protocol now makes the ledger write mandatory in unattended runs.","remediation":"Ship the header-only ledger or bootstrap it for TARGET_KIND=live; delete .gitignore:149 instead of negating.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1188"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"state_consistency","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":580,"code_snippet":".rejection_rationale = $rat | .follow_up = $fu | ... | .status = \"rejected\"","reasoning_trace":"op_reject rewrites only its own row; the decided row's supersede_proposed_by (set :610) is never cleared; :601 then refuses every later agent supersede. Validator :656-657 only checks .supersedes on the named row; :681 forbids clearing the pointer later. Reproduced end to end; validator exit 0 on the dangling ledger.","finding":"rejecting a proposed replacement strands the decided row behind a dangling pointer; validator accepts it and forbids the repair","critique":"Permanent dead end in append-only team state.","remediation":"Clear the pointer in the same reject write; validator requires the named row to be proposed; allow X->null when the named row is rejected.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-662","CWE-20"]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"concurrency","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":655,"code_snippet":"rm -f -- \"$from\"","reasoning_trace":"acquire_lock :628 locks the live target only; pending read :629, unconditional rm :655; the worktree writer's lock is under its own PROJECT_ROOT/.run (:203-207) so the two never contend. Code path confirmed; race reproduced by the review, not re-run here.","finding":"import neither locks nor coordinates with the pending file's writer; concurrent rows are deleted or imported twice","critique":"The one flow designed for parallel worktree agents loses or duplicates rows silently.","remediation":"Lock next to the pending file so both checkouts contend; re-read after the lock; rm only if sha256 matches what was imported.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-362"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"access_control","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":250,"code_snippet":"if has file; then TARGET=\"$(o file)\"; TARGET_KIND=\"fixture\"; ... return 0; fi","reasoning_trace":"--file returns before ci_blocked (:261) and the worktree redirect (:255). Reproduced: CI=1 and LOA_HOOK_CONTEXT=1 writes to grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml via --file exit 0.","finding":"--file naming the live ledger bypasses the CI/hook refusal and the worktree redirect","remediation":"Resolve --file absolutely; treat the live path as live; apply ci_blocked unless under tests/ or BATS tmp.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-284"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":652,"code_snippet":"awk ... - \"$p\" > \"$tmp2\"; chmod 0644 \"$tmp2\"; mv -f \"$tmp2\" \"$p\"","reasoning_trace":"--rewrite paths checked with -f only; no containment, .. or symlink check (contrast artifact_path :289-295). Reproduced: file outside the project rewritten; symlink replaced by a regular file. --from (:655) deleted likewise.","finding":"import --rewrite rewrites any writable path, follows and replaces symlinks; --from deletes any path that validates","remediation":"Containment under PROJECT_ROOT/MAIN_ROOT, refuse -L, reuse artifact_path checks.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-22","CWE-59"]}
{"id":"SEC-007","category":"security","criterion":"output_encoding","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/grimoire-index.sh","line":189,"code_snippet":"def s: tostring | gsub(\"[[:cntrl:]\\u2028\\u2029]\"; \" \") ...","reasoning_trace":"Compared the three emitters of ledger text. Hook :69-70 replaces <, >, backticks and strips C1; grimoire-index :189 and dec-write-lib op_list :677-678 do not. Reproduced: a summary containing </untrusted-content> and <invoke name=\"Bash\"> appears verbatim in --tsv, INDEX.md and list --format md; render-templates.md:105-112 pastes the md unfenced into the PR body; decisions.md:52 makes it the confirming session's preview.","finding":"untrusted ledger text reaches INDEX.md, grimoire-index.json, the PR body and SDD/PRD appendices with <, >, backticks and C1 intact","remediation":"One shared sanitiser (the hook's clean); fence the preview and PR-body table.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-116","OWASP-LLM01"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":656,"code_snippet":"if ((if ($s | type) == \"string\" then $byid[$s] else null end) | (. != null and .supersedes == $r.id)) | not then ...","reasoning_trace":"The rule checks only that the named row supersedes this one, not its status; reproduced exit 0 on a ledger where it points at a rejected row.","finding":"validator accepts a supersede_proposed_by pointer to a rejected row","remediation":"Require .status == \"proposed\" on the named row.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20"]}
{"id":"ARCH-003","category":"architecture","criterion":"state_consistency","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":606,"code_snippet":"if is_operator_call && ! is_unattended; then r=... .status = \"superseded\" ...","reasoning_trace":"Operator path supersedes the old row at proposal time; reject (:560) does not restore; :599 forbids superseding a non-decided row. Reproduced: decision absent from the active view after rejecting the replacement.","finding":"operator supersede then reject of the replacement loses the decision","remediation":"Set supersede_proposed_by on the operator path too and flip on confirm, or restore on reject.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-662"]}
{"id":"SEC-008","category":"security","criterion":"attribution","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":537,"code_snippet":".decided_by_ref = (if .decided_by_ref == null and $ref != \"\" then $ref else .decided_by_ref end)","reasoning_trace":"Flatline/dissent rows always carry decided_by_ref (:330-332, required by validator :640-643) so the operator's ref is dropped and decided_by becomes flatline/dissent; conversely an interactive new --answer-ref session:... pre-seeds the pointer and survives confirm (dissent DISS-C-006).","finding":"confirm keeps a pre-existing decided_by_ref: flatline/dissent rows never record operator; agent-seeded refs become the operator's evidence","remediation":"Always record the operator's ref on confirm; keep the proposing artifact ref in a separate field.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-284"]}
{"id":"SEC-009","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":157,"code_snippet":"sess=\"${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID:-${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID:-}}\"","reasoning_trace":"Staleness by other-session needs the env var; absent, a marker stays fresh for the TTL and confirm's refusal (:509) never names /decisions clear-unattended; present and caller-chosen, it disables the marker (reproduced).","finding":"marker staleness depends on the caller's environment; repair text omits the fix","remediation":"Time-based staleness or hook-written session id; name clear-unattended in the refusal.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-807"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation_consistency","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":261,"code_snippet":"if why=\"$(ci_blocked)\"; then die \"refused: ${why} is set; the ledger is never written from CI or a hook ...\"","reasoning_trace":"Check precedes the pending branch; reproduced CI=1 new --pending refused, contrary to header :22-23 and karpathy-principles.md:33-38.","finding":"ci_blocked also refuses --pending and worktree writes","remediation":"Apply only when TARGET_KIND == live.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-1068"]}
